In Classic WoW, most warlocks were seen with voidwalkers because **voidwalkers are the default pet**—they spawn automatically upon leveling to 10, while succubi require learning the *Summon Succubus* spell (available at level 20) and are less intuitive for new players. Additionally, voidwalkers’ *Suffering* (AoE taunt) and *Consume Shadows* (OOC regen) were highly valuable for solo leveling and dungeon pulls, especially before players optimized pet usage. Succubi, though stronger DPS-wise, lacked reliable threat management and required more micromanagement—making voidwalkers the practical, beginner-friendly choice. [end of text]


